gRPC hello world: the client sends a name and the server replies with a greeting.

Depends
-------

Install grpcio and grpcio-tools with your distribution packages (python3-grpc-tools),
or in a virtualenv, either with pip:

$ python3 -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate
$ pip install -r requirements.txt

or with uv (creates .venv and opens a shell with it activated):

$ make shell

(requirements.txt is generated from pyproject.toml with "make requirements.txt")


Compile proto
-------------

$ python -m grpc_tools.protoc -I. --python_out=. --grpc_python_out=. hello.proto


Run server
----------

$ ./server.py


Run client
----------

$ ./client.py localhost 2000


Demo
----

$ ./demo.sh    # requires tmux
